  more_label: "MORE · HOW IT IS BUILT",
  p1_details: "<ul><li><b>Architecture.</b> Express/TypeScript and PostgreSQL 17 on my own server. I moved it off Cloud Run, Supabase and Firebase in two weeks. Each user's data is isolated at row level, and I check backups by restoring them. The front end is React and TypeScript, and a Python engine for market structure runs in a separate worker thread.</li><li><b>Agents on LangGraph.</b> Graphs with a fixed shape and a human approval step wherever the agent would change something that belongs to the trader. Proposals from the chat wait for “Save”, and the session plan takes effect only after the trader accepts it. Code computes results, stops and risk. The model interprets them and has no way to write to anything that touches money.</li><li><b>Models chosen by measurement.</b> One registry for 51 AI roles, so I can switch a model without a deploy. Today the platform runs on Gemini, chosen on test cases.</li><li><b>Quality.</b> Over 260 test cases for prompts in promptfoo, each written to fail before the fix. Every model call leaves a trace in Langfuse. I audit the mentor's answers regularly and keep a fix backlog. On top of that there are more than 600 test files (vitest, Playwright, pytest) and CI gates for prompt quality and security.</li><li><b>Apple apps in Swift.</b> An iPhone app prepared for the App Store, with Sign in with Apple, account deletion in the app and consent before the first use of AI. A Mac menu-bar companion, signed and notarized, that updates itself. A shared Swift 6 package, and both apps in Polish and English.</li><li><b>Product and security.</b> Stripe subscriptions, OIDC sign-in with a hand-off to the native apps, SSRF protection, rate limits and a GDPR data export. My own MCP server with OAuth 2.1 and PKCE. A futures broker connection that writes the trade journal by itself and checks the trader's risk rules live.</li><li><b>Removing what does not work.</b> I cut a feature that cost up to six minutes and 14 cents per trade and gave no evidence in 354 reviews. I halved the mentor prompt and the answers got better. A shared cost ledger reserves budget before every model call.</li><li><b>R&amp;D on Microsoft Foundry (since November 2026).</b> In a separate test environment I am testing a knowledge layer for the next version: search over the Academy lessons with Azure AI Search, Foundry IQ and an agent, compared with today's pgvector and Gemini on the same questions. Only Academy content and a test account, no customer data.</li></ul><p><a href=\"/projects/trader-ai-assistant\">Behind the scenes: how I’m building it →</a></p>",
  p2_title: "Deep Mentor",
