  p2_desc: "The deep-analysis agent inside Trader AI Assistant. It is a ReAct agent with 10 tools and long-term memory, which I moved from the Claude Agent SDK to LangGraph. Before it answers, it reads what the platform knows about the trader: the current focus, hypotheses with evidence for and against, and past corrections. It quotes that memory instead of answering from general knowledge. Search combines full-text and vector retrieval, and measurement raised recall from 23% to 85%.",
  p2_stack: "LangGraph ReAct · 10 tools · pgvector + full-text search (RRF) · structured memory",
  p2_details: "<ul><li><b>Memory written by the platform.</b> After each trading day, agent steps update the trader's memory, and the mentor cites it in later analyses.</li><li><b>Hybrid search, measured.</b> pgvector combined with full-text search through Reciprocal Rank Fusion and checked on a set of real questions. Recall went from 23% to 85%.</li><li><b>Cost by design.</b> Short summaries in prompts instead of raw data, expensive deep runs only when the trader asks, and a memory health check that runs 13 tests without a model and without spending tokens.</li></ul>",
  p3_title: "audit-mentor · finding-ledger",
